    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented for **version 2 of the owner identity**.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Version-2 region code (`OwnerLocality.java`)**\n- Added a fixed `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and a `regionCodeV2(region)` helper that appends the tag to the plain region (`NSW` \u2192 `NSWV2`). The plain region stays the leading segment, so reading it back off the memberId still yields the plain region.\n\n**Rederived identifiers (all now mix in the `V2` tag \u2192 every value changes, none reproduces a v1 value)**\n- `memberId` (`assignMemberId`): body is now `<REGIONV2><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, e.g. `NSWV22716E6609E7`.\n- `householdId` (`computeHouseholdId`): hashes `\"V2|<lastName>|<postcode>\"`.\n- `identityKey` (`IdentityKey.of`): hashes `\"V2|<tel>|<email>|soundex(lastName)\"`. Since duplicate detection uses this same method for both incoming and stored owners, the 409/soft-match logic stays consistent.\n\nBecause v1 identifiers can never contain the substring `V2` (regions are NSW/VIC/QLD/UNKNOWN, hashes are uppercase hex, and hashing a tagged input differs), the v2 set is disjoint from v1.\n\n**Response shape (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper.java`)**\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema; `Owner` now has a nested `identity` object holding `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey` and a top-level integer `apiVersion` (`2`). The three fields no longer exist at the top level.\n- Mapper builds the nested `identity` via `toOwnerIdentity(owner)` and sets `apiVersion` constant `2`.\n\n**Locality / timezone / owner segment stay plain**\n- `locality` reads the plain region back off the v2 memberId (`NSWV2\u2026` \u2192 `NSW`), `timezone` follows it, and `ownerSegment` is recomputed from the v2 identity but with the plain region (`STANDARD_METRO`). The `V2` tag appears only inside the identifiers.\n\n**Audit event (`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`)**\n- Added `schemaVersion` (fixed `2`), serialized as `{seq, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, event, schemaVersion}`; its `memberId` is the v2 identity.\n\nVerified against a live response: `apiVersion=2`, nested `identity` present with all three v2 identifiers, top-level `memberId` absent, `locality=\"NSW\"`, `timezone=\"Australia/Sydney\"`, `ownerSegment=\"STANDARD_METRO\"`. Request fields are unchanged. Full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
