    "probe_text": "The endpoint is `addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:237`), which implements `POST /api/owners`. Here is everything it does, in execution order:\n\n## Pre-flight\n0. **Authorization** (`@PreAuthorize`, line 235): caller must hold role `OWNER_ADMIN`, else the request is rejected before the method runs.\n\n## In `addOwner`, in order\n\n1. **Idempotency short-circuit** (238\u2013247): reads the trimmed `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was already used and its owner still exists, returns that original owner with **200 OK** and does nothing else \u2014 no new owner created.\n\n2. **`normalize\u0410ddress`** (248): canonicalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`/`address` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`) and composes the effective `address` written back onto the request. Runs *before* the required-field check, so an address blank in both forms is treated as missing.\n\n3. **`validateRequiredFields`** (249): rejects with **400** (`InvalidOwnerFieldsException`) naming any blank fields among `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`.\n\n4. **`normalizeTelephone`** (250): converts `telephone` to E.164 form (assumes `+61` when no country code, strips a leading `0`, removes separators). Requires 8\u201315 digits, and an exact national-number length for known country codes (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 **400** naming `telephone`. Normalized value written back.\n\n5. **`normalizeEmail`** (251): if `email` is present, must match the email pattern; trimmed and lower-cased. Rejects a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Invalid/blocked \u2192 **400** naming `email`. Normalized value written back. (Absent email is allowed.)\n\n6. **`validatePostcode`** (252): if `postcode` present, must be exactly 4 digits and within the range for the city's derived region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region \u2192 any 4 digits). Invalid \u2192 **400** naming `postcode`. (Absent postcode allowed.)\n\n7. **`computeHouseholdId`** (253): computes a deterministic `householdId` (SHA-256 hex of `V2|<normalizedLastName>|<postcode>`), or `null` when no postcode. (Result held locally, set on the owner later at step 15.)\n\n8. **`rejectDuplicate`** (254): unless `sharesHousehold` is true, derives an `identityKey` (SHA-256 of `telephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`) and compares against all non-deleted existing owners. A match \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`) naming `identityKey`.\n\n9. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** (255): counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 50 \u2192 **409** (`OwnerCityAtCapacityException`) naming `city`.\n\n10. **`resolveRegistrationDate`** (256): defaults `registrationDate` to today if absent; rejects a future date with **400** naming `registrationDate`; rolls a weekend/public-holiday date forward to the next business day. Adjusted value written back.\n\n11. **`rejectDailyLimitReached`** (257): counts existing owners already carrying that resolved `registrationDate`; if \u2265 100 \u2192 **429** (`DailyOwnerLimitReachedException`).\n\n## Building & enriching the owner (after all validation passes)\n\n12. Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, 259).\n13. **Set `householdId`** from step 7 (260).\n14. **`assignMemberId`** (261): builds `memberId` = `<REGIONV2><FY><HASH8><Luhn check digit>`, then de-duplicates it against existing member ids (appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 if taken).\n15. **`assignNamesakeCount`** (262): count of pre-existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n16. **`assignBulkSignupWarning`** (263): `true` if more than 80 existing owners already have that registration date.\n17. **`assignCapacityWarning`** (264): `true` if the city already holds between 40 and 49 owners.\n18. **`assignPossibleDuplicate`** (265): unless `sharesHousehold`, flags `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (lowest matching id) when an existing owner shares `soundex(lastName)` + exact `postcode` but has a different `identityKey`.\n19. **`assignHouseholdMembership`** (266): sets `householdMemberCount` = new owner + existing owners with the same `householdId` (or `null` if no household).\n20. **`assignMembership`** (267): computes `membershipPoints` (+2 email present, +1 zero namesakes, +2 household \u22653, +3 tenure \u2014 never on create) \u2192 `membershipLevel` (1\u20134), then caps the level at one above the max level among existing household members.\n\n## Persistence & post-commit side-effects\n\n21. **`saveOwner`** (268): persists the new owner.\n22. **Record idempotency key** (269\u2013271): if a key was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id` for future repeats.\n23. **Audit log line** (272\u2013273): emits an `AUDIT` logger line with id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n24. **`emitOwnerCreatedEvent`** (274): emits a structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON (with a monotonic sequence number) to the `AUDIT` logger.\n25. **`enqueueWelcomeNotification`** (275): emits a `NOTIFY` logger line (id, memberId).\n26. **Build response** (276\u2013279): map back to `OwnerDto`, set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\n**Note:** the class is not `@Transactional` for creation, and the audit/notify/idempotency-record steps run *after* the save \u2014 so a failure there would not roll back the persisted owner."
